From d0979e4dbe7df6912d21a5891eaca01778a6b2b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:56:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cursor: split cache creation from cache read and stop faking
 tool results

Follows the stale-resume/parallel-tools commit. Three findings from probing
the production gateway on 15.204.914.214.

Cache creation was never reported. openAIUsagePayload carried only
prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens, so a cold turn that paid to fill the
cache was indistinguishable from one that never cached: 42,760 prompt
tokens, 18,717 of them read, and nothing at all said about the 24,041
written. usage.Detail already tracked CacheCreationTokens for the internal
stats; only the wire payload dropped it. It now carries
prompt_tokens_details.cache_creation_tokens, the name the rest of the
repository already parses.

The Anthropic side dropped it too. extractOpenAIUsage read only
cached_tokens and subtracted it from input_tokens, so /v1/messages clients
saw cache_read_input_tokens and never cache_creation_input_tokens. It now
splits both counters out of the prompt, matching how Anthropic reports the
three as disjoint, and omits a counter that is zero.

The workspace built-ins reported a broken environment. Their diagnostic came
back as Shell with no exit status, Write succeeded but the following Read
could not find the file, and Glob with "No exec result":

- The workspace is rooted at the process home directory. The service runs as
  a nologin account whose home does not exist and cannot be created by that
  account, so every MkdirAll failed, was ignored, and the model was handed a
  path nothing could write to. It now falls back to a base that works.
- handleWriteArgs answered every write with success even when nothing
  landed, which is what made the following read look like the failure. It
  now answers with the real outcome.
- An exec variant the trimmed proto has no case for decoded to nil and the
  stream was closed with no result, which the harness surfaces as "No exec
  result" or a shell with no exit status and the model retries for whole
  segments. It now throws with text the model can act on.
- The note telling the model these built-ins are unavailable was only added
  to claude runs that attached client tools, so a plain chat never saw it
  and spent a segment on Shell and Glob before declaring the environment
  broken. Every run gets it now.

Serving Read from the workspace was tried and reverted: ReadSuccess_Data is
the reference-image channel, and putting a text file through it made the
provider reject the turn with a 400 on every attempt.
